      "narration": "Every state, including Maryland, adopted a model law listing provisions that individual health policies must contain and others they may contain. The required provisions protect the insured and may be worded differently only if the insurer’s version is at least as favorable. Rosa’s disability policy and Marcus’s individual medical plan therefore share the same skeleton. This lesson covers the provisions about the contract and the premium; Lesson 16 covers the claim clocks; Lesson 17 covers the optional provisions and renewability. The exam tests these as day counts and rules, so learn each number with its purpose.",
