      "title": "Entire contract and changes",
      "narration": "The entire contract provision states that the policy, including any endorsements and the attached application, is the whole agreement. Nothing said outside those documents is part of the contract. No statement by the applicant can be used against her unless it is in the attached application. Changes to the policy are valid only if approved by an executive officer of the insurer and endorsed on or attached to the policy. A producer cannot change the policy or waive any of its provisions. If Theo promises Rosa a benefit the policy does not contain, the promise is not part of the contract, and he has exposed himself to liability.",
