      "narration": "A grace period gives the insured time to pay a late premium while coverage continues. The uniform provision requires at least seven days for weekly premium policies, ten days for monthly premium policies and thirty-one days for all other modes, such as quarterly or annual. A claim during the grace period is paid, although the insurer may deduct the overdue premium. If the premium is still unpaid when the grace period ends, the policy lapses as of the due date. Marcus pays monthly, so a premium due on the first is late on the eleventh, and his policy lapses if nothing arrives by then.",
