      "narration": "A lapsed policy can come back. If the insurer accepts a late premium without requiring a reinstatement application, the policy is reinstated when the premium is accepted. If the insurer requires an application and issues a conditional receipt for the premium, the policy is reinstated when the insurer approves the application, or automatically on the forty-fifth day after the receipt date if the insurer has not disapproved it in writing. A reinstated policy covers accidents immediately but covers sickness only if it begins more than ten days after reinstatement. The insurer and insured otherwise have the same rights they had before the lapse.",
